From 21fefed09f0c690bd113e5d8da2e798a0884043d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stephen Leary <stephen@terriblefire.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 20:35:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/6] XC95XL: check every argument and the JEDEC file before
 the device

From a review of the first change:
- One file per run. Its action, the JEDEC file (complete up to ETX,
  fuse count, a C checksum that matches, the device name) and -e are
  all checked before anything is sent to the device; -e with a read or
  verify, W (no erase), unknown actions and unopenable files are refused.
- A read that cannot write its file exits 1.
- Before erasing or programming, check the IR capture as iMPACT does
  (000xxx01, bits 4:2 not checked).
- Waits are timed with the monotonic clock.
- JEDEC parser: header and N-field writes stay inside their buffers.
- gpiod cable: Init() fails when a JTAG line could not be requested; the
  constructor stops at the first failure and closes the chip once.
---
